  "note": "Plan 16 task 7 (slice 6 goldens): ruling 9's 'sum' combine rule, pinned through pack data. The log is multi-fighter5-barbarian3-mastery's log (Fighter 5 Champion -> Barbarian 3 Berserker, the same decisions and the same five equipped weapons), with one difference: seq 2 pins the engine fixture pack mastery-sum-house-rule 1.0.0. That pack has no entities. Its one override replaces the core system's /multiclass/masteryCount ('max' in packages/content/src/static/system.ts) with 'sum', so the per-character index's system() combines the mastery.grant counts by adding them (derive/attacks.ts masteryCap). The 'max' result for the same log stays pinned by multi-fighter5-barbarian3-mastery and is not repeated here. Hand table (SRD data): the fighter-weapon-mastery-count row extra is 4 at fighter level 5 (3 at levels 1-3, 4 from level 4); the barbarian-weapon-mastery-count row extra is 2 at barbarian level 3 (2 at levels 1-3). So masteryCount = 4 + 2 = 6 (max would be 4). The cap is shared and filled in class order. The Fighter's three recorded picks (longsword sap, greatsword graze, warhammer push; its 4th slot was never re-picked) fill slots 1-3. The Barbarian's two picks fill slots 4-5: handaxe vex and greataxe cleave. Under 'max' the greataxe pick is over the cap; here it is honoured, so the greataxe row gains mastery cleave and one slot stays free. Unchanged by the rule: level 8, prof +3; STR 15 + Soldier 2 + fighter 4 ASI 2 = 19 (+4); HP 71 = fighter 10+2, 4 x (6+2), then barbarian 3 x (7+2); Extra Attack 2. Greataxe: to-hit 4+3 = +7, damage 1d12 + 4 slashing.",
